WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.345
♫

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:14.889
Most people hosting a
travel show want to do it.

00:00:14.889 --> 00:00:17.726
They love doing it.
They have a sense of adventure.

00:00:18.268 --> 00:00:19.936
That's not me.

00:00:20.729 --> 00:00:21.688
Okay, this is crazy.

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:23.398
Oh god.

00:00:23.398 --> 00:00:25.275
I think I'm feeling a
heart attack coming on.

00:00:25.275 --> 00:00:27.152
I think they got the
wrong guy for the job.

00:00:29.946 --> 00:00:32.907
I said to my agent,
"I'm definitely not the person for this show."

00:00:32.991 --> 00:00:35.952
This is one cowboy that
will never have his own movie.

00:00:36.494 --> 00:00:37.245
Woah.

00:00:37.245 --> 00:00:37.954
[Horse whinnies]

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:40.915
This has taken me
all over the world.

00:00:40.915 --> 00:00:43.168
Places I'd probably would
never had gotten to

00:00:43.168 --> 00:00:44.502
if it hadn't been for the show.

00:00:44.794 --> 00:00:46.087
The Maldives.

00:00:46.087 --> 00:00:49.632
That was the longest trip
of all the places to get to.

00:00:49.632 --> 00:00:50.925
A lot of flying.

00:00:50.925 --> 00:00:53.595
Traveling, again.
Not one of my favorite things.

00:00:53.595 --> 00:00:54.971
Woah.

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:56.389
Sweaty palms.

00:00:56.848 --> 00:00:58.933
We wanted Eugene to
experience paradise

00:00:58.933 --> 00:01:01.644
and to see how he felt
when he was here.

00:01:01.644 --> 00:01:04.647
It's not as easy as sitting
on the couch with a bowl of popcorn.

00:01:04.647 --> 00:01:08.526
I promise you you'll see
a lot of wildlife tonight.

00:01:08.526 --> 00:01:09.486
[Eugene laughs]

00:01:09.486 --> 00:01:12.113
Going into a jungle at night
in Costa Rica,

00:01:12.113 --> 00:01:14.157
you know, looking for
poisonous snakes.

00:01:14.157 --> 00:01:15.408
Let's say you get bit?

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:17.160
About an hour you're going to have.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:18.912
- I have an hour to get to the hospital.
- That's right.

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:20.622
And the hospital is how far?

00:01:20.622 --> 00:01:21.748
Fourty five minutes away.

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:22.707
Ahhh.

00:01:22.707 --> 00:01:24.334
Why are we still here?
[Guide laughs]

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:27.754
Yeah, I'm still kind of
wondering why I'm doing it.

00:01:28.379 --> 00:01:30.799
I was in Lapland.
The artic circle.

00:01:30.799 --> 00:01:31.674
Ice floating.

00:01:31.674 --> 00:01:34.427
I could not be more out of
my comfort zone

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:36.262
than I am right this second.

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:36.930
Reindeer meat.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.598
Okay, here we go.

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:40.016
Then dog sleds.

00:01:40.016 --> 00:01:41.392
Well, it's been nice knowing you.

00:01:41.392 --> 00:01:42.393
[Handler calls out to dogs]

00:01:42.393 --> 00:01:44.771
Oh my god.

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:48.316
South Africa. Wow.
I never really had any desire

00:01:48.316 --> 00:01:50.693
to go on a safari or whatever.

00:01:50.693 --> 00:01:52.320
I thought I had seen it all.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:53.530
At the zoo.

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:56.533
Oh my!

00:01:56.533 --> 00:01:58.743
I have to say, it's been
a bit of an eye opener for me.

00:01:58.743 --> 00:02:02.288
Um, I haven't seen the view
yet to be honest.

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:03.790
I'm looking out now.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:06.626
I'm doing some things
I would never have done.

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:09.045
That's a long way down Tony.

00:02:09.045 --> 00:02:11.422
I'm set in a show that looks gorgeous.

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:15.426
The cinematography that's
going into making the series

00:02:15.426 --> 00:02:16.845
is incredibly important,

00:02:16.845 --> 00:02:18.721
we've got drone teams in the air,

00:02:18.721 --> 00:02:21.307
we've got a great director of
photography with his camera team

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:25.687
and we want to transport the viewer
to these completly amazing locations.

00:02:25.687 --> 00:02:27.730
There's a lot of talent and
a lot of great work

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:30.692
putting this show together and
making it look as good as it does.

00:02:30.692 --> 00:02:32.777
In spite of the fact that
I'm the guy in the middle of it.

00:02:33.069 --> 00:02:35.196
No matter what country I'm in,
I always know that

00:02:35.196 --> 00:02:37.574
there's going to be some
laughs and some good times.

00:02:37.574 --> 00:02:40.034
It's really about the people
and the culture.

00:02:40.034 --> 00:02:42.120
You're kind of looking at
what everybody's doing

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.913
and finding out how
they're doing it.

00:02:43.913 --> 00:02:44.914
Wow!

00:02:44.914 --> 00:02:47.333
And what the background is
and what their history is.

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:50.587
A part of our culture and our language
will always be with you. Thank you.

00:02:50.587 --> 00:02:53.631
This is amazing. This is,
this is really special.

00:02:53.631 --> 00:02:56.259
So at my age right now

00:02:57.218 --> 00:02:57.886
Oh god.

00:02:57.886 --> 00:03:02.140
I think it's something I
needed to be forced to do.

00:03:02.473 --> 00:03:04.601
I can't believe I did it.

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:06.269
[Laughs]

00:03:06.269 --> 00:03:06.728
Woo.

00:03:06.728 --> 00:03:08.730
And I've even surprised myself.

00:03:09.397 --> 00:03:11.274
Mush you huskies!

00:03:11.274 --> 00:03:11.983
Woo hoo hoo!

00:03:11.983 --> 00:03:14.068
I'm the luckiest guy in the world.

00:03:14.068 --> 00:03:14.611
[Laughs]

00:03:14.611 --> 00:03:15.945
I'm glad it happened.

00:03:15.945 --> 00:03:17.572
And I never thought I would say that.

